    "id": "introduction",
    "group": "Getting started",
    "title": "Introduction",
    "description": "Vortex Studio runs Luau scripts against its scene and multiplayer runtime.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Overview",
        "body": "The runtime exposes a small Roblox-style API: Instances, engine services, Vector3, Color3, CFrame, signals, tasks, tweens, and remotes. If an API is not listed here, assume this build does not expose it."
      },
      {
        "heading": "A first script",
        "body": "Services are reached through game:GetService. Instances use the same method-call syntax as ordinary Luau userdata.",
        "code": "local Workspace = game:GetService(\"Workspace\")\nlocal platform = Workspace:WaitForChild(\"Platform\")\n\nplatform.Anchored = true\nplatform.Position = Vector3.new(0, 4, 0)\nplatform.Color = Color3.fromRGB(92, 170, 255)"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Version scope",
        "body": "This reference covers the Vortex Studio build released on 1 September 2026. Later builds may add or change members."
      }
    ]
